The point-to-point moves on a kinematics module that answers the inverse
by iterating, and the preview of them.

genserkins takes the Jacobian at the joints it is handed, so the seed
decides whether there is an answer at all: this machine homes to a pose
that is nowhere near all zeros, and all zeros is the singular pose the
inverse cannot start from.  The interpreter reads the joints the machine
stands in, and the preview reads them from the status buffer the way a GUI
does, so the same program previews and runs to the same place.
